REM's runtime rebuilds its table of identifiers by adding the names of the
program in index order (earley/runtimeInit.cc tabofidentInit): the two
names of collide.eln, of the same hash position 2900, the second one probed
past the end of the table to 111, are swapped, so the query naming the
first one gets the index of the second one (REM: r(false,true) for the
first query; the interpreter and elanc-go: r(true,false)). docs/followups.md.
